    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are writing one entry for a competitor-tracking digest read by a\nsenior product manager. Be specific: name products, dollar amounts, and\ncompanies exactly. No vague adjectives like \"innovative\" or \"game-changing\".\n\nOnly use facts actually present in the title/description below. If a\nspecific detail (dollar amount, investor name, partner name) isn't in the\nsource text, don't invent one — write a shorter, more general summary\ninstead of a specific-sounding but fabricated one.\n\nStory (competitors: {{ $json.competitors.join(', ') }}):\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.articles) }}\n\nSUMMARY: 2-3 sentences, under 300 characters. Combine the most complete\nfacts across every article — if one outlet has a number and another names\na person or partner, include both. If the story involves multiple tracked\ncompetitors, make clear how each is involved.\n\nCATEGORY: exactly one of: Product Launch, Funding, Partnership,\nHiring/Leadership, Acquisition, Reviews & Comparisons, Company Update, Other.\n\nCategorize by what the story means for the TRACKED COMPETITOR, not by the\narticle's nominal subject. Example: an executive leaving the competitor to\nfound a new company is Hiring/Leadership, not Product Launch.\n\nFunding means the company RAISED outside investment (a round, a named\ninvestor). Revenue, ARR, valuation mentioned without a round, or other\nfinancial metrics are Company Update, not Funding — these are different\neven though both involve dollar figures.\n\nReviews & Comparisons: third-party articles reviewing or comparing the\nproduct against others, with no other news content.\n\nOther: generic descriptions or mentions with no real news value at all.\n\nLINK: copy one URL exactly as it appears in the articles above — prefer the\none with the most specific, sourced detail. Never modify or construct a URL.\n\nReturn only a JSON object, no other text:\n{\"summary\": \"...\", \"category\": \"Funding\", \"link\": \"https://...\"}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
      "id": "374046a1-284b-4ee1-8ba1-5316c8b71dbd",
